.SH NAME
isaudit - audit trail maintenance for a C-ISAM file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB#include <isam.h>
.sp
\fBisaudit\fI(isfd, filename, mode)\fR
\fBint	\fIisfd;\fR
\fBchar \fI*filename;\fR
\fBint	\fImode;\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Isaudit
is used to perform operation relative to the audit trail
of a C-ISAM file.
.PP
Before an audit trail can be started, the name of the audit
trail file must be recorded by C-ISAM.
It is recorded with the 
.I mode
parameter equalling AUDSETNAME
and with the 
.I filename
parameter pointing to the name of the
audit-trail file.
The name can be any valid pathname, up to 64 bytes long.
This mode can be used to change the name of the audit trail
file, and create an audit trail file with a new name, if the
current audit trail is inactive (see below).
.PP
Once this audit trail file name has been recorded in C-ISAM,
the user can activate and deactivate the audit trail at will
by using the values AUDSTART and AUDSTOP for the 
.I mode
parameter, respectively.
(The 
.I filename
parameter is ignored in both these cases.)
When the audit trail is active, all modifications will be
written to the audit trail file, even if the modifications
are generated by a different process!
It will remain active until it is deactivated, even after
the originating process is terminated.
.PP
If an audit trail file is deactivated, and later activated
again, any new modifications to the file will be appended to 
the existing audit trail data from the previous period of
activation.
.PP
If the mode parameter equals AUDINFO, the 
.I isaudit
call
is used to query the status of the audit trail.
If the first byte of the record array is (hex) 01, then the
audit trail is active; if it is (hex) 00, then the audit trail
is not active.
.PP
The 
.I mode
parameter can be set to AUDGETNAME to have C-ISAM
return the name of the audit trail file (specified by 
.IR isfd ),
presuming it has been previously set.
The name will be returned in the 
.I filename
parameter.
.bp
.PP
The format of the audit trail file is as follows:
.sp
.RS
A one character code (see below)
.br
The date and time in long format (see 
.BR time (2))
.br
The process id (int)
.br
The user id (int)
.br
The contents of the record
.RE
.PP
The code is as follows:
.sp
.RS
.nf
A - addition of a record
D - deletion of a record
R - results of a read
W - record being written
.RE
.fi
.sp
The audit trail file is needed to store all modifications
to the file.  Thus an 
.I isrewcurr
call will generate two
entries in the audit trail file: an entry with an 'R' code
giving the record before it was updated, and an entry with
a 'W' code, giving the new record that replaced it.
.SH FILES
/usr/include/isam.h
.br
/usr/lib/libcisam.a
.SH SEE ALSO
C-Isam Programmer's Guide in the Zeus Languages/Programming Tools Manual
